<h1 class="article-title">Declaration Signed to Establish the Liepāja Sustainable Industry Centre</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>A significant declaration has been signed on the creation of the Liepāja Sustainable Industry Centre in the Liepāja Special Economic Zone (Liepāja SEZ), bringing together several strategically important private investment projects focused on green energy, smart manufacturing and innovation.</p><p>The signatories include private investors implementing development projects — Van Oord, Euroports, Smulders, CIS Liepāja, GI Termināls and Fokker Next Gen Latvia — together with the Liepāja SEZ Authority, Liepāja City Council, the Investment and Development Agency of Latvia (LIAA) and Riga Technical University.</p><p>The joint declaration seeks to give these projects the highest priority on the government agenda and secure necessary state support through simplified procedures and approvals, access to financial instruments and infrastructure investment. The projects will contribute to the sustainability of Latvia’s economy, establish new high-tech industries and promote GDP growth and industrial development.</p><p>The Liepāja Sustainable Industry Centre aims to become a central player in green energy and innovative technologies in the Baltic region. Total planned investment could exceed EUR 4 billion between 2025 and 2035.</p><p>Planned projects:</p><ol><li>Offshore wind support base and heavy cargo terminal at the Port of Liepāja — infrastructure to support construction of Baltic Sea wind farms and manufacturing plants for oversized structures near port berths. Implemented by Van Oord, Euroports and Smulders.</li><li>Hydrogen plant and terminal — production of hydrogen using renewable energy sources. Implemented by CIS Liepāja.</li><li>Sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) plant — SAF production to help the aviation sector transition to more environmentally friendly energy sources. Implemented by GI Termināls.</li><li>Hydrogen-powered aircraft production — manufacturing passenger aircraft at Liepāja Airport to help decarbonise aviation. Implemented by Fokker Next Gen Latvia.</li><li>CO₂ export terminal — storage and transport of carbon dioxide captured from industrial and energy-related emissions. Implemented by GI Termināls.</li></ol><p>Liepāja SEZ CEO Uldis Hmieļevskis noted that the scale of private investment is unprecedented not only in the Liepāja SEZ but in Latvia as a whole. It will establish entirely new industries based on green hydrogen and oxygen production, CO₂ transport and storage, and the recovery of thermal energy, while creating opportunities for other businesses to use these resources as raw materials.</p><p>“By choosing Liepāja as the location for their projects, investors demonstrate Latvia’s determination to develop green energy and smart manufacturing. The Liepāja Sustainable Industry Centre will enable the region to become a leader in renewable energy and industrial innovation, attract further investment and create jobs in other sectors. Attracting investments of this scale requires professional cooperation among all parties, including the state, municipality and educational institutions. That is why we have agreed to treat the individual projects as one whole and present them as the Liepāja Sustainable Industry Centre,” Uldis Hmieļevskis emphasised.</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority is working to connect these projects and investors, identifying additional synergies and opportunities for new projects. Hydrogen is planned as a feedstock for SAF production and fuel for Fokker Next Gen aircraft, while CO₂ will also be needed for SAF production. Transforming the former Liepājas Metalurgs steelworks into a green industrial park will help attract other manufacturers that can use H₂, CO₂, O₂ and thermal energy as inputs.</p><p>Riga Technical University plays an important role in developing sustainable industries by providing educational and research programmes through RTU Liepāja Academy. Cooperation with the Investment and Development Agency of Latvia to facilitate project implementation, as well as the involvement of Liepāja City, is equally important.</p><p>About the Liepāja Special Economic Zone Authority:</p><p>The Liepāja SEZ Authority provides a high-quality, attractive business environment and promotes the coordinated development of the SEZ territory under clear conditions. It attracts investors in smart, sustainable, high-value-added industries, particularly manufacturing, green energy and technology, creating skilled jobs with competitive salaries.</p></div>
